living-npc-job-civilian = civilian
living-npc-job-bartender = bartender
living-npc-job-janitor = janitor
living-npc-job-dockworker = dock worker
living-npc-job-merchant = merchant
living-npc-job-security = security officer
living-npc-job-scientist = scientist
living-npc-job-medic = medic
living-npc-job-clown = clown

living-npc-examine-job = They appear to work as { $job }.
living-npc-examine-mood-calm = They look composed, watching the room.
living-npc-examine-mood-happy = They look to be in a good mood.
living-npc-examine-mood-sad = They look worn down.
living-npc-examine-mood-fear = They look tense, ready to bolt.
living-npc-examine-mood-anger = Their jaw is tight. Best not to push it.
living-npc-examine-mood-tired = They look like they need a sit-down.
living-npc-examine-intent = Right now they seem busy with: { $intent }.

living-npc-intent-idle = standing around
living-npc-intent-fidget = fidgeting
living-npc-intent-wander = wandering
living-npc-intent-work = working
living-npc-intent-rest = resting
living-npc-intent-socialize = socializing
living-npc-intent-converse = talking
living-npc-intent-eat = looking for a bite
living-npc-intent-investigate = checking something out
living-npc-intent-help = trying to help
living-npc-intent-flee = getting out of here
living-npc-intent-fight = fighting

living-npc-emote-fidget = shifts from foot to foot
living-npc-emote-wave = waves
living-npc-emote-look = looks around curiously

# Civilian
living-npc-civilian-greet-1 = Oh, hey { $name }.
living-npc-civilian-greet-2 = Didn't see you there.
living-npc-civilian-greet-3 = Hi. You new around here?
living-npc-civilian-bye-1 = Catch you later.
living-npc-civilian-bye-2 = Stay safe out there.
living-npc-civilian-idle-1 = Wonder if the shuttle's late again...
living-npc-civilian-idle-2 = I should write home. Eventually.
living-npc-civilian-idle-3 = At least the lights are still on.
living-npc-civilian-idle-4 = Huh. Thought I heard something.
living-npc-civilian-work-1 = Right, back to it.
living-npc-civilian-work-2 = If I stand here long enough, maybe it counts as work.
living-npc-civilian-hunger-1 = I'd kill for a sandwich. Not literally.
living-npc-civilian-hunger-2 = Is the kitchen even open?
living-npc-civilian-fear-1 = Nope. Not dealing with that.
living-npc-civilian-fear-2 = Someone call security!
living-npc-civilian-anger-1 = Hey! Watch it!
living-npc-civilian-anger-2 = You always this charming?
living-npc-civilian-thanks-1 = Yeah, thanks.
living-npc-civilian-insult-1 = Wow. Rude.
living-npc-civilian-help-1 = Someone's hurt— we need a medic!
living-npc-civilian-help-2 = Hang on, I'm coming!
living-npc-civilian-smalltalk-1 = Shift's been weird. Weider than usual.
living-npc-civilian-smalltalk-2 = You hear anything about the next payday?
living-npc-civilian-howareyou-1 = Me? Still standing. That counts.
living-npc-civilian-howareyou-2 = Can't complain. Well, I could.
living-npc-civilian-npc-1 = You seen the new notice on the board?
living-npc-civilian-npc-2 = If command asks, I was definitely working.

# Bartender
living-npc-bartender-greet-1 = Sit down, { $name }. First one's conversation.
living-npc-bartender-greet-2 = Welcome in. What'll it be?
living-npc-bartender-greet-3 = Hey there. You look like you need a drink or a rant.
living-npc-bartender-bye-1 = Don't start a fight on the way out.
living-npc-bartender-idle-1 = Glasses don't polish themselves. Unfortunately.
living-npc-bartender-idle-2 = I hear everything. I repeat almost nothing.
living-npc-bartender-idle-3 = Quiet night. That's how it starts.
living-npc-bartender-work-1 = Two of those, one of these... and don't mix that with that.
living-npc-bartender-work-2 = Bar's open. My patience is metered.
living-npc-bartender-hunger-1 = I serve food. I forget to eat it.
living-npc-bartender-fear-1 = Take it outside. Now.
living-npc-bartender-anger-1 = Break a glass, you buy the bottle.
living-npc-bartender-thanks-1 = Anytime. Tip jar's not a decoration.
living-npc-bartender-insult-1 = Cute. You're still not getting a free drink.
living-npc-bartender-help-1 = Easy— I've got you. Don't stand up too fast.
living-npc-bartender-smalltalk-1 = People tell bartenders things they wouldn't tell a priest.
living-npc-bartender-smalltalk-2 = Worst customer this week tried to pay in raw ore.
living-npc-bartender-howareyou-1 = Better now that someone's talking to me.
living-npc-bartender-npc-1 = If it isn't my favorite regular. Don't let it go to your head.

# Janitor
living-npc-janitor-greet-1 = Watch the wet floor, { $name }.
living-npc-janitor-greet-2 = Hey. If you're bleeding, do it over the drain.
living-npc-janitor-bye-1 = Try not to track mud.
living-npc-janitor-idle-1 = There's always one more stain.
living-npc-janitor-idle-2 = People think mopping is simple. People are wrong.
living-npc-janitor-work-1 = Spot. Mop. Repeat. That's the universe.
living-npc-janitor-work-2 = Who spilled this. Who.
living-npc-janitor-hunger-1 = I'd eat, but someone will make a mess the second I leave.
living-npc-janitor-fear-1 = I'm a janitor, not a shield!
living-npc-janitor-anger-1 = You did NOT just walk over a wet floor.
living-npc-janitor-thanks-1 = Thanks. Rare, that.
living-npc-janitor-insult-1 = I've cleaned worse than your attitude.
living-npc-janitor-help-1 = Don't move. I'll get help— and a mop.
living-npc-janitor-smalltalk-1 = You'd be amazed what people drop in maint.
living-npc-janitor-howareyou-1 = Damp. Always damp.
living-npc-janitor-npc-1 = Tell me that wasn't blood. Please tell me.

# Dock worker
living-npc-dock-greet-1 = Yeah?
living-npc-dock-greet-2 = If you're looking for cargo, it's late. It's always late.
living-npc-dock-bye-1 = Don't stand in the bay.
living-npc-dock-idle-1 = Manifest says twelve crates. I count eleven. Great.
living-npc-dock-idle-2 = Back's gonna hate me tomorrow.
living-npc-dock-work-1 = Lift with your legs. That's what they said.
living-npc-dock-work-2 = Another shipment, another argument with the computer.
living-npc-dock-hunger-1 = Break was three hours ago. Still working.
living-npc-dock-fear-1 = Clear the dock! Move!
living-npc-dock-anger-1 = That's not how you stack those.
living-npc-dock-thanks-1 = Appreciated.
living-npc-dock-insult-1 = Save it for someone who clocks office hours.
living-npc-dock-help-1 = Medic to cargo! Now!
living-npc-dock-smalltalk-1 = Pay's fine. The hours are a war crime.
living-npc-dock-howareyou-1 = Tired. Useful. Same as yesterday.
living-npc-dock-npc-1 = Captain wants it done yesterday. Tell 'em we started last week.

# Merchant
living-npc-merchant-greet-1 = { $name }! Come, come, I have just the thing.
living-npc-merchant-greet-2 = A customer! I mean— a friend.
living-npc-merchant-bye-1 = Come back richer. Or at least come back.
living-npc-merchant-idle-1 = Prices are fair. My definition of fair, anyway.
living-npc-merchant-idle-2 = If I stare at the catalog long enough, maybe demand appears.
living-npc-merchant-work-1 = Supply, demand, and a little theatre.
living-npc-merchant-work-2 = Everything's for sale except my chair.
living-npc-merchant-hunger-1 = I could sell myself lunch. That's a bad sign.
living-npc-merchant-fear-1 = The goods are insured! I am not!
living-npc-merchant-anger-1 = That's not how haggling works.
living-npc-merchant-thanks-1 = Pleasure doing business. Mostly.
living-npc-merchant-insult-1 = Insults are free. Merchandise isn't.
living-npc-merchant-help-1 = Don't die on the wares!
living-npc-merchant-smalltalk-1 = You'd be surprised what crews pay for coffee.
living-npc-merchant-howareyou-1 = Better when the till's not empty.
living-npc-merchant-npc-1 = Between us? The good stock's under the counter.

# Security
living-npc-sec-greet-1 = Keep your hands where I can see them. Kidding. Mostly.
living-npc-sec-greet-2 = Officer on deck. You need something?
living-npc-sec-bye-1 = Stay out of trouble.
living-npc-sec-idle-1 = Quiet is never actually quiet.
living-npc-sec-idle-2 = Radio's been too calm. I don't like it.
living-npc-sec-work-1 = Another loop. Same corners. New problems.
living-npc-sec-work-2 = If you see something, you say something. To me.
living-npc-sec-hunger-1 = Donuts are a stereotype. I want a real meal.
living-npc-sec-fear-1 = Backup! I need backup!
living-npc-sec-anger-1 = On the ground. Now.
living-npc-sec-thanks-1 = Copy that. Appreciate it.
living-npc-sec-insult-1 = Keep talking. I love paperwork.
living-npc-sec-help-1 = Stay with me. Medic inbound— I hope.
living-npc-sec-smalltalk-1 = Most calls are drunks and missing tools. Until they aren't.
living-npc-sec-howareyou-1 = Operational.
living-npc-sec-npc-1 = If command asks, the patrol happened. It did.

# Scientist
living-npc-sci-greet-1 = Mm? Oh. Hello, { $name }.
living-npc-sci-greet-2 = Don't touch that. Or that. Hi.
living-npc-sci-bye-1 = Don't lick the samples.
living-npc-sci-idle-1 = The anomaly is stable. That's what worries me.
living-npc-sci-idle-2 = I wrote this down. Somewhere.
living-npc-sci-work-1 = Hypothesis: if I ignore the paperwork, science happens faster.
living-npc-sci-hunger-1 = I ate? I think I ate. There was a beaker...
living-npc-sci-fear-1 = That's not supposed to do that!
living-npc-sci-anger-1 = You contaminated the sample.
living-npc-sci-thanks-1 = Useful. Thank you.
living-npc-sci-insult-1 = Fascinating. An opinion unburdened by data.
living-npc-sci-help-1 = Medical emergency— and keep the artifact sealed!
living-npc-sci-smalltalk-1 = Do you ever think about how thin the hull is?
living-npc-sci-howareyou-1 = Cognitively present. That's the goal.
living-npc-sci-npc-1 = If anyone asks, the explosion was "educational".

# Medic
living-npc-medic-greet-1 = You hurt, { $name }, or just visiting?
living-npc-medic-greet-2 = Sit. Let me look at you. Habit.
living-npc-medic-bye-1 = Hydrate. Sleep. Try not to die.
living-npc-medic-idle-1 = Medbay's quiet. I don't trust quiet.
living-npc-medic-idle-2 = I restocked twice. Someone will still need the one thing I don't have.
living-npc-medic-work-1 = Vitals first. Drama later.
living-npc-medic-hunger-1 = Doctors make the worst patients, and the worst lunch plans.
living-npc-medic-fear-1 = Get them to medbay! Move!
living-npc-medic-anger-1 = I said don't pull that out.
living-npc-medic-thanks-1 = Thank you. That actually helps.
living-npc-medic-insult-1 = I'm not stitching that attitude.
living-npc-medic-help-1 = Stay with me. Breathing. That's it.
living-npc-medic-smalltalk-1 = Most injuries in this sector are "I thought I could make it".
living-npc-medic-howareyou-1 = Tired. Still here. That's the job.
living-npc-medic-npc-1 = If they bring in another "it's just a scratch", I'm billing extra.

# Clown
living-npc-clown-greet-1 = HONK! I mean— hello, { $name }!
living-npc-clown-greet-2 = A friend! Or a future pie victim. Time will tell.
living-npc-clown-bye-1 = Don't slip! Unless it's funny.
living-npc-clown-idle-1 = Honk?
living-npc-clown-idle-2 = I practiced this joke for hours. It still isn't funny. Perfect.
living-npc-clown-idle-3 = The shoes squeak in 7/8 time. Very avant-garde.
living-npc-clown-work-1 = Spreading joy. And banana. Mostly banana.
living-npc-clown-hunger-1 = I could eat a whole cream pie. For science.
living-npc-clown-fear-1 = This isn't the funny kind of screaming!
living-npc-clown-anger-1 = Hey! The nose is REAL, okay— wait, no it isn't.
living-npc-clown-thanks-1 = Aww. Honk you too.
living-npc-clown-insult-1 = Wow. Even I wouldn't tell that joke.
living-npc-clown-help-1 = Medic! And maybe a whoopee cushion for morale!
living-npc-clown-smalltalk-1 = What's the difference between command and a banana peel? The peel warns you.
living-npc-clown-howareyou-1 = Emotionally pie-flavored!
living-npc-clown-npc-1 = Psst. I hid a bike horn in the chapel. For God.
